        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.wisdomlib.org/cities/rosewood-heights-96844"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The village was incorporated in 1958 as part of the suburban boom around the Metro East area near St. Louis.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.wisdomlib.org/cities/rosewood-heights-96844"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Rosewood Heights sits in northwestern Madison County, within the Greater St. Louis Metro East region.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rosewood_Heights%2C_Illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Its borders touch Bethalto to the east, Wood River to the south, East Alton to the west, and Cottage Hills to the north.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rosewood_Heights%2C_Illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Water from the community drains northwest toward the East Fork of the Wood River, which joins the Mississippi at East Alton.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
